  "text": "Death is as common, if not more so, than life. Despite this, death and decay are considered subjects of the macabre, and those willing to dive headfirst into the fascinations they invoke are necromancers. These occult spellcasters seek the ever-changing borders of life and death, manipulating magic of vitality and void to suit their will. The undead both serve and cower before them.\n\nNecromancer"
